  "notes": "Sony BRAVIA 4K GB (BRAVIA_ATV2_UC, MediaTek mt5891), US/Canada firmware\nAndroid TV 9, build PTT1.190515.001.S54 672201, security patch 2022-01-05\nSame platform and build as examples/sony-xbr-x900e; this list confirms it on a second model.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/sony-bravia-4k-gb-us/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/sony-bravia-4k-gb-us/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (restore.sh's default).\nLive TV / input app: com.sony.dtv.tvx. Keep it: it also plays every HDMI input.\nKeep: com.sony.dtv.tvinput.*, braviasync* (HDMI-CEC), remotepairing, rcpowerkey, uinputservice,\nimeproxy, sonysystemservice, settingsprovider, all com.mediatek.* and mtktvapi.agent.\nAlready disabled at the factory: com.sony.dtv.actionmenu.plugin.harmony. Not in this list.\n\nNotes from this firmware:\n- ADB: the Developer options switch is labelled \"ADB debugging\", not \"USB debugging\". Port 5555\nstays closed until it is on.\n- com.google.android.tungsten.setupwraith is installed but did not take Home: build-and-install.ps1\nlanded Home on com.gathin.tvhome first time with only com.google.android.tvlauncher disabled.\nHide com.sony.dtv.tvx and com.sony.dtv.tvxlauncher.programguide in config.xml and leave\nlive_tv_package empty if you have no antenna; Inputs lists HDMI 1-4 (with CEC names) and Video 1/2.\n- The stock launcher's \"Free Live TV\" / \"Top Selling\" rows and the top banner come from\ntvlauncher itself and stay until it is replaced.\n- Tested the same day it was applied: Home, the Input menu, HDMI inputs and the new launcher all\nwork. Not yet lived with for several days, and not yet tested across a reboot.\nACR viewing tracker",
